@title: EXTRACT returns the value, not its caption
# expect-output: price=[$24.50]
# expect-output: total=[42 items]
# expect-output: shipping=[Free]
# expect-output: order=[1234]
# expect-output: status=[Shipped]
# expect-output: weight=[2 kg]
# expect-output: name=[Manul Plush]
# expect-output: gift=[Gift wrap]
# expect-output: byid=[$61.20] eta=[Tuesday] line=[Subtotal: $55.00]
STEP 1: Captions in their many forms
    NAVIGATE to @SITE@/extract.html
    EXTRACT the 'Price' into {price}
    EXTRACT the 'Total' into {total}
    EXTRACT the 'Shipping' into {shipping}
    EXTRACT the 'Order' into {order}
    EXTRACT the 'Status' into {status}
    EXTRACT the 'Weight' into {weight}
    PRINT "price=[{price}] total=[{total}] shipping=[{shipping}] order=[{order}]"
    PRINT "status=[{status}] weight=[{weight}]"
STEP 2: Text that is not a caption comes back whole
    EXTRACT the 'Manul Plush' into {name}
    EXTRACT the 'Gift' into {gift}
    PRINT "name=[{name}] gift=[{gift}]"
STEP 3: By id or test id
    EXTRACT the 'order-total' into {byid}
    EXTRACT the 'eta' into {eta}
    EXTRACT the 'summary-line' into {line}
    PRINT "byid=[{byid}] eta=[{eta}] line=[{line}]"
DONE.
